  "thePurpose": "The counterexample slice of RECON-W43.2: does the system read a counterexample against a claim's scope, and does it propose a narrowing only when the evidence supports one?",
  "theNote": "The dataset is split into train, validation and test. The test cases are the held-out ones: the runner builds a FRESH store per case, so no case can leak into another, and the test split is measured once. The set carries the mission's own worked example: a penguin REFUTES 'All birds fly' and does NOT refute 'Most birds fly under ordinary conditions' - the system cannot decide that from the text, so it asks instead of proposing a narrowing.",
  "theLanguageNote": "The slice's decisions are LANGUAGE-INDEPENDENT by construction: the reading depends on the evidence relation and on whether a condition was recorded, not on the words. The Russian subset therefore measures that the pipeline carries the text through unchanged and reads the structure, not that it understands Russian.",
