  "theTruth": "The expectations are the TRUTH, not the system's current answers. Where the system cannot decide from the text — whether a counterexample falls inside the scope a claim states — the truth is that it does not decide, and the case expects SCOPE_UNRESOLVED. The human truth for those cases is 'the observation does not bear on the claim in its scope'; the system's vocabulary has no word for that, and SCOPE_UNRESOLVED is the closest honest one: it neither refutes nor supports, and it asks."
}
